        "Board connections. For each director and statutory auditor listed in a firm's annual business report, we coded career histories to identify positions held in central government ministries and agencies (grade 3 or above), the presidential office (secretary level or above), the National Assembly, the prosecution service (chief prosecutor level or above), the judiciary (presiding judge or above), the Fair Trade Commission, the Financial Services Commission and Financial Supervisory Service, and the National Tax Service. A director is classified as connected if any such position was held in the ten years before the year of observation. Officials are assigned to the administration under which they last served, and politicians to the party with which they were last affiliated.",
